  "_source": "Vendor facts come from platform.claude.com/docs \u2014 pricing, models/overview, prompt-caching, batch-processing, effort. Fetched 2026-07-03 for the seven models then current: knowledge_cutoff from the models/overview \"Reliable knowledge cutoff\" row, and every min_cacheable_prefix from that same day's prompt-caching \"minimum cacheable prompt length\" list so the whole column shares one provenance; no projection reads min_cacheable_prefix today, so re-verify the column at the next refresh. Refreshed 2026-07-24: claude-opus-5 added from pricing, models/overview, effort and prompt-caching \u2014 list rates match claude-opus-4-8 at $5 in / $25 out, min_cacheable_prefix 512 (the lowest of any current model), knowledge cutoff 2026-05, all five effort levels \u2014 and claude-opus-4-8 moved to the vendor's legacy table on the same date. effort_available follows the effort doc: every model defaults to high, xhigh is Opus 4.7 and later plus Sonnet 5 and Fable 5, max is Opus 4.6 and later plus Sonnet 4.6 and later and Fable 5; a row with no effort-doc entry lists low/medium/high, the levels carrying no documented restriction. The 0.5 batch_discount is the API-wide Batches rate from batch-processing, not a per-model figure. claude-opus-4-5 and claude-sonnet-4-5 are carried for allowlist parity only: no vendor spec block was sourced for them in this refresh, so their vendor-fact fields and price are null. release_date is recorded only where a vendor snapshot date is published. Long-context refreshed 2026-08-09 from pricing \u201cLong context pricing\u201d: Claude 4.6 and later models (and Claude Mythos Preview) include the full 1M-token window at standard pricing \u2014 no premium \u2014 so every row that read 1000000 now records context_window as the 200000 runtime default and gains context_variants['1m'], reachable via the <id>[1m] selector, whose context_window is 1000000 and whose price duplicates that row's base list rates (rate identity: the 1M window is not a distinct price point, so the variant rate equals the base rate). premium_applies_above_input_tokens is the 200000 runtime-default threshold even though no premium is charged above it. Per the schema's contextVariant the variant carries exactly {context_window, price, premium_applies_above_input_tokens}; cross_family_rank and every other row-level fact stay on the base row.",
  "_unit": "USD per 1,000,000 tokens",
